-- demo/theGUI/gTable.exw
-- ======================
--
--DEV 
--  See demo\theGUI\gTable.exw for an example of saving/restoring user-modified layouts. [DEV not yet done!]
--
--  An gTable is a Phix/pGUI invention, expressly written for pwa/p2js,
--  but of course it can be freely used for strictly desktop-only purposes.
--
-- TODO: add a 1-hour-lifespan gTable.ini ...:
--  COL_SORT: note that {{3,2,1}} restores the actual sort order, whereas {t,f,t} sets which sorts are allowed, with an error
--            occurring should the latter not exactly match the number of COLUMNS (and NULL treated as false, since it is).
--      (for instance I often bemoan the lack of "taskmgr.exe /blah" to open it at say cpu/memory/network traffic)
--      (             to minimise the disruption of an unexpected crash)
--      (             filedump uses the same table for several tabs, and switching should not lose your place on each tab)
--
--  Save/Restore user-modified table layouts:
--  ========================================
--
--  This program also demonstrates the use of (in this case a 1-hour lifespan) 
--  gTable.ini to save/restore any user modifications to the table layout, ie
--  by clicking and dragging things about to sort/reorder/resize the table.
--  The 1-hour lifespan minimises confusion when re-running days/weeks later.
--  You can of course delete/edit the gTable.ini whenever/however you like.
--
